From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] NickelOS: setup names the computer with the first account

Settings > About can rename the computer (0083), but setup never asked, so
every NickelOS computer was "localhost" until someone renamed it. The
first account's screen now has a Computer name field under "Your name",
filled in as the name is typed: "Dresden's Latitude 5510" from the
person's first name and the computer's model (nickel-hostnamed's
HardwareModel), or "Dresden's Laptop" (or Desktop, Tablet, Computer) when
the firmware's model is a placeholder or a desktop's motherboard name.
Once edited, it stays as typed. On Create, the name is set first
(org.nickelos.Hostname1's SetName, which nickel-hostnamed allows from the
sign-in screen until an account exists), then the account is made; a name
with no character a hostname can hold gets Settings' error, and any other
failure leaves the name for Settings. Later accounts ("Add person") don't
see the field.

The screen's own wording, hardcoded English until now, moves into
ui_chromeos_strings.grd, so it can be translated, with the new strings.

